WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:02.047
Lolly Tools

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.143
Powerfully reproducible assets & tools.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.191
Deterministic, fast, open-source platform

00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:13.269
- bring your own brand.

00:00:14.038 --> 00:00:15.843
Try it now.

00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:19.068
lolly-tools runs in the browser and

00:00:19.124 --> 00:00:21.569
installs as an app.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:25.125
Nothing you make ever leaves your device

00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:26.969
without your say.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.522
lolly-art is the same app on a blank

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:31.719
brand.

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:35.366
Desktop, mobile and command-line builds

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:37.919
are on the releases page.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:40.468
Read first.

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:43.181
The platform is explained at

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:46.948
lolly-tools/info, with one door each for

00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:50.101
creators, builders and operators, a

00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:53.309
quickstart, and the trust pages that back

00:00:53.395 --> 00:00:55.544
each claim with the mechanism that

00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:57.294
enforces it.

00:00:58.084 --> 00:01:01.193
We built Lolly for ourselves.

00:01:01.993 --> 00:01:05.329
SUSE needed thousands of on-brand files,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.552
each with its name sealed inside, made

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:10.903
without handing anything to outside

00:01:10.967 --> 00:01:12.345
services.

00:01:13.136 --> 00:01:16.088
So we built a tool that does all of it on

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.418
the device, and released it as open

00:01:19.529 --> 00:01:22.370
source, like everything else we make.

00:01:23.146 --> 00:01:26.286
We keep maintaining it because we use it

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:27.694
every day.

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:31.317
There is no obligation: everything here

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.919
works with or without us.

00:01:35.065 --> 00:01:37.391
What is Lolly Tools

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.600
A platform that hosts a library of small,

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:44.858
focused tools that produce deterministic

00:01:44.919 --> 00:01:46.744
creative assets.

00:01:47.532 --> 00:01:50.543
Users need no design skill, no vendor

00:01:50.604 --> 00:01:53.892
lock-in and no internet to render, and the

00:01:53.954 --> 00:01:56.782
platform is designed to add premium

00:01:56.842 --> 00:01:59.788
production-quality rendering certainty to

00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:01.645
variable data.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:05.811
It's also your personal DAM - every logo,

00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:08.626
palette, font and upload lives in an

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:11.513
on-device catalog, hydrated and

00:02:11.618 --> 00:02:14.218
supercharged by your design system and

00:02:14.282 --> 00:02:15.469
tools.

00:02:16.248 --> 00:02:19.368
Tools can be used via a:

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.188
Web app - installable offline progressive

00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:24.196
web app

00:02:25.238 --> 00:02:29.493
Mobile and Desktop installable packages.

00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:36.050
and of course, the Command Line - plus a full-screen terminal UI «TUI».

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:41.093
Why deploy Lolly in your organization?

00:02:41.878 --> 00:02:44.555
Hard-coded constraints of design

00:02:44.611 --> 00:02:46.068
decisions.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:55.100
Free, open-source platform - the engine, every shell, the schemas and docs are MPL-2 point 0.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:06.775
Tools and assets are just data: bring your own brand content «SUSE's tool & asset packs are proprietary - see Licensing & structure».

00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:10.870
Unlimited scale, No SaaS fees.

00:03:11.673 --> 00:03:15.499
Low-or-Zero server costs: Lolly uses local

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.319
device compute.

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:21.321
Builds for Mac, Windows, Linux, iOS,

00:03:21.381 --> 00:03:24.045
Android, web and the command line.

00:03:24.425 --> 00:03:30.500
Huge format support - 37 in, 40 out «21 round-trip».

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:58.425
Export: SVG · EPS · CMYK EPS · EMF · DXF · PDF · Print PDF «CMYK» · PPTX · PNG · Animated PNG · JPEG · WebP · Animated WebP · AVIF · TIFF · CMYK TIFF · ICO · PSD · EXR · Radiance HDR · MP4 · WebM · GIF · Animated SVG · MP3 · M4A · WAV · Opus · HTML · MD · TXT · CSV · JSON · ICS · VCF · ZIP.

00:03:58.775 --> 00:04:14.200
Import adds layered PSD · PSB · XCF, HEIC, MOV · Lottie, GLB · glTF, audio & tracker «OGG · FLAC · MIDI · MOD» and live designs from Illustrator · InDesign · Figma · Penpot.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:21.600
EXR and Radiance HDR are floating-point HDR masters «via host-codec».

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:33.375
Plus design tokens & palettes - import DTCG and Tokens Studio; export DTCG · ASE · GPL · CSS variables.

00:04:33.725 --> 00:04:45.600
Print-ready output: CMYK PDF & TIFF, physical units, bleed, crop/registration marks, colour bars and press «FOGRA/SWOP» profiles.

00:04:46.336 --> 00:04:50.244
Infinite deterministic media creation.

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:58.425
Renders and exports 100% offline - the shells need no network at render time.

00:04:58.775 --> 00:05:10.625
«The optional hosted services - MCP agent endpoint, Content Credentials CA - are separate opt-ins; see docs/server-surface-md.»

00:05:11.387 --> 00:05:14.218
Full command-line support.

00:05:14.995 --> 00:05:18.067
Save tokens, tell your model to try Lolly

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.245
first!

00:05:20.376 --> 00:05:22.287
What this is not

00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:26.376
A general-purpose design tool

00:05:27.268 --> 00:05:29.745
It does include an open canvas - the

00:05:29.803 --> 00:05:32.890
Design tool - but even there, colours,

00:05:32.955 --> 00:05:35.479
type and assets conform to the brand

00:05:35.539 --> 00:05:38.836
globals, so free arrangement never becomes

00:05:38.926 --> 00:05:40.770
off-brand output.

00:05:41.565 --> 00:05:44.765
See docs/positioning-md for the full

00:05:44.827 --> 00:05:46.719
market comparison.

00:05:47.854 --> 00:05:50.093
Repository layout

00:05:51.088 --> 00:05:54.236
lolly is an umbrella repo: the app core

00:05:54.296 --> 00:05:57.332
lives here, and each shippable unit is a

00:05:57.403 --> 00:05:59.204
git submodule hosted under

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:01.895
github-com/lolly-tools.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.862
Every submodule is mounted at its original

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.285
path, so the monorepo builds and runs

00:06:09.351 --> 00:06:11.494
exactly as before.

00:06:12.272 --> 00:06:15.093
Code example omitted.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:21.150
Critical separation: engine/ knows nothing about SUSE.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:39.975
Brand-specific content lives in brand packs «brands/suse - private; brands/lolly-start - the blank starter brand», brand-agnostic tools in community/; the shells, services, engine and docs are MPL-2 point 0.

00:06:40.325 --> 00:06:59.650
The repo-root tools/ and catalog/ paths every script and shell consumes are profile views built by scripts/use-profile-ts from profiles-json - switch brands with npm run profile:suse / npm run profile:start.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:09.525
Keeping each unit in its own repo lets it ship on its own cadence while the umbrella pins a known-good combination.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.956
Architectural commitments

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:16.869
These decisions are settled.

00:07:17.631 --> 00:07:20.405
Changing any of them is a major

00:07:20.484 --> 00:07:25.125
undertaking: Declarative tools.

00:07:25.475 --> 00:07:30.400
A tool is a manifest + template + assets.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:37.050
Inputs are declared in the manifest, not inferred from template tokens.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:47.225
hooks-js is an optional escape hatch for tools that need imperative behavior «chart-js rendering, QR encoding».

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:51.109
Tools and assets are data, not bundled

00:07:51.193 --> 00:07:52.318
code.

00:07:53.092 --> 00:07:56.154
Clients sync them from a signed manifest

00:07:56.236 --> 00:07:57.643
URL.

00:07:58.451 --> 00:08:01.562
New tools and assets don't require app

00:08:01.604 --> 00:08:02.868
updates.

00:08:03.636 --> 00:08:05.993
Capability bridge.

00:08:06.771 --> 00:08:10.103
Tools never touch the filesystem, network

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:13.368
or DOM-outside-template directly.

00:08:14.145 --> 00:08:17.068
They call a versioned host.

00:08:17.845 --> 00:08:20.394
* API.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.781
This is what makes the same tool work in

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.445
browser, Tauri and CLI.

00:08:27.235 --> 00:08:30.493
Stable asset ID'S forever.

00:08:31.292 --> 00:08:35.794
suse/logo/primary is a contract.

00:08:36.597 --> 00:08:39.544
Never reuse, never rename.

00:08:40.339 --> 00:08:43.073
Version in the manifest, never in the

00:08:43.148 --> 00:08:44.194
path.

00:08:44.575 --> 00:08:48.225
URL mode is first-class.

00:08:48.575 --> 00:08:53.575
Every input must be expressible as URL params.

00:08:53.925 --> 00:09:00.875
CLI mode = headless DOM «jsdom» + URL mode + file output.

00:09:01.225 --> 00:09:03.850
One render path.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.325
Storage via the bridge.

00:09:07.675 --> 00:09:12.350
Tools call host-state-save«» / host-state-load«».

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:18.775
The bridge picks IndexedDB «web», filesystem «Tauri» or memory «CLI».

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:22.150
Tools never know which.

00:09:22.902 --> 00:09:25.293
Maturity tags.

00:09:26.072 --> 00:09:28.958
Every tool declares status: official |

00:09:29.021 --> 00:09:31.593
community | experimental.

00:09:32.369 --> 00:09:34.933
Experimental tools watermark their

00:09:34.995 --> 00:09:36.319
exports.

00:09:37.085 --> 00:09:39.602
This is the structural answer to the

00:09:39.657 --> 00:09:42.644
"brand approved by default" risk.

00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:45.614
Getting started

00:09:46.609 --> 00:09:50.643
